<quiz>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_THELIVINGWORLD_MCQ_Q01 - Taxonomic categories in ascending hierarchy of mango</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p>Refer to the given diagram showing the hierarchical arrangement of taxonomic categories in ascending order:</p>
<div style="text-align: center; margin: 15px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 470" width="380" height="470" style="background-color: #fcfcfc; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; border-radius: 8px;">
    <defs>
      <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#1e3a8a"/>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <!-- Kingdom -->
    <rect x="90" y="20" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
    <text x="190" y="45" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#0369a1" text-anchor="middle">Kingdom</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow -->
    <line x1="190" y1="85" x2="190" y2="65" stroke="#1e3a8a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
    
    <!-- Category II -->
    <rect x="90" y="85" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
    <text x="190" y="110" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#b45309" text-anchor="middle">Category II</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow -->
    <line x1="190" y1="150" x2="190" y2="130" stroke="#1e3a8a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
    
    <!-- Class -->
    <rect x="90" y="150" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
    <text x="190" y="175" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#0369a1" text-anchor="middle">Class</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow -->
    <line x1="190" y1="215" x2="190" y2="195" stroke="#1e3a8a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
    
    <!-- Category I -->
    <rect x="90" y="215" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
    <text x="190" y="240" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#b45309" text-anchor="middle">Category I</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow -->
    <line x1="190" y1="280" x2="190" y2="260" stroke="#1e3a8a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
    
    <!-- Family -->
    <rect x="90" y="280" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
    <text x="190" y="305" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#0369a1" text-anchor="middle">Family</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow -->
    <line x1="190" y1="345" x2="190" y2="325" stroke="#1e3a8a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
    
    <!-- Genus -->
    <rect x="90" y="345" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
    <text x="190" y="370" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#0369a1" text-anchor="middle">Genus</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow -->
    <line x1="190" y1="410" x2="190" y2="390" stroke="#1e3a8a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
    
    <!-- Species -->
    <rect x="90" y="410" width="200" height="40" rx="6" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
    <text x="190" y="435" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#0369a1" text-anchor="middle">Species</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p>Identify the categories marked as <strong>Category I</strong> and <strong>Category II</strong>, and determine the correct combination of taxa representing these ranks for mango (<em>Mangifera indica</em>):</p>
      ]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Step 1: Identify Category I and Category II in the taxonomic hierarchy.</strong><br/>The universal ascending taxonomic hierarchy begins at species and ascends as: Species &rarr; Genus &rarr; Family &rarr; Order &rarr; Class &rarr; Phylum or Division &rarr; Kingdom. Hence, the rank positioned between Family and Class is Order (Category I), and the rank positioned between Class and Kingdom is Division for plants or Phylum for animals (Category II).</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Determine the taxonomic classification of mango (<em>Mangifera indica</em>).</strong><br/>According to the standard classification of mango (<em>Mangifera indica</em>):
Genus: <em>Mangifera</em><br/>
Family: Anacardiaceae<br/>
Order: Sapindales<br/>
Class: Dicotyledonae<br/>
Division: Angiospermae</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Correlate the designated categories with the corresponding taxa.</strong><br/>Category I corresponds to Order, which is represented by Sapindales in mango. Category II corresponds to Division, which is represented by Angiospermae in mango.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Check and conclude the final answer.</strong><br/>The correct match is that Category I is Order (represented by Sapindales) and Category II is Division (represented by Angiospermae).</p>
      ]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Category I is Order (represented by Sapindales) and Category II is Division (represented by Angiospermae)</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Category I is Class (represented by Dicotyledonae) and Category II is Division (represented by Angiospermae)</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Category I is Order (represented by Polymoniales) and Category II is Phylum (represented by Chordata)</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Category I is Family (represented by Anacardiaceae) and Category II is Class (represented by Dicotyledonae)</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
