  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_THELIVINGWORLD_MCQ_Q02 - Directional trends of shared characteristics in hierarchy</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p>The diagram below depicts the taxonomic hierarchy along with two opposing directions of progression, Direction A and Direction B:</p>
<div style="text-align: center; margin: 15px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 540 380" width="540" height="380" style="background-color: #fbfcfe; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 8px;">
    <defs>
      <marker id="arrowUp" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#047857"/>
      </marker>
      <marker id="arrowDown" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#6d28d9"/>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    
    <!-- Left Arrow: Direction A -->
    <line x1="55" y1="330" x2="55" y2="45" stroke="#047857" stroke-width="4" marker-end="url(#arrowUp)"/>
    <text x="55" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#047857" text-anchor="middle">Direction A</text>
    <text x="55" y="355" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#065f46" text-anchor="middle">(Species &rarr; Kingdom)</text>
    
    <!-- Central Hierarchy Stack -->
    <g transform="translate(130, 20)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="280" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="24" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Kingdom</text>
      
      <rect x="15" y="46" width="250" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="70" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Phylum / Division</text>
      
      <rect x="30" y="92" width="220" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="116" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Class</text>
      
      <rect x="45" y="138" width="190" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="162" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Order</text>
      
      <rect x="60" y="184" width="160" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="208" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Family</text>
      
      <rect x="75" y="230" width="130" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="254" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Genus</text>
      
      <rect x="90" y="276" width="100" height="38" rx="5" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="300" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e40af" text-anchor="middle">Species</text>
    </g>
    
    <!-- Right Arrow: Direction B -->
    <line x1="485" y1="45" x2="485" y2="330" stroke="#6d28d9" stroke-width="4" marker-end="url(#arrowDown)"/>
    <text x="485" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#6d28d9" text-anchor="middle">Direction B</text>
    <text x="485" y="355" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#5b21b6" text-anchor="middle">(Kingdom &rarr; Species)</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p>Which of the following statements correctly describes the biological attributes observed along Direction A and Direction B?</p>
      ]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Step 1: Analyze the biological trend along Direction A (ascending progression).</strong><br/>Direction A indicates moving up the taxonomic hierarchy from species to kingdom. As one goes higher from species to kingdom, the number of common characteristics shared among organisms goes on decreasing. The higher the category, the more general the characters become, and determining the relationship to other taxa at the same level becomes increasingly complex.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Analyze the biological trend along Direction B (descending progression).</strong><br/>Direction B indicates moving down the taxonomic hierarchy from kingdom to species. Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share. Therefore, descending from kingdom towards species results in a progressive increase in shared fundamental similarities and specific morphological traits.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Conclude the valid comparative relationship.</strong><br/>Direction A represents a decrease in the number of shared common characteristics, while Direction B represents an increase in the number of shared fundamental similarities.</p>
      ]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Direction A represents an increase in the number of shared common characteristics, while Direction B represents a decrease in morphological similarities.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Direction A represents a decrease in the number of shared common characteristics, while Direction B represents an increase in the number of shared fundamental similarities.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Direction A represents an increase in morphological similarities, while Direction B represents an increase in taxonomic complexity.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Direction A represents a decrease in the difficulty of determining relationships, while Direction B represents a decrease in shared characteristics.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
